    "rationale": "Competitive inhibition of UGT2B7 (UDP-glucuronosyltransferase) by a small-molecule inhibitor. The inhibitor:substrate molar ratio is [I]/[S] = 35.2/2353.5 ≈ 0.015, and fractional activity under competitive inhibition is v_i/v_0 = [S]/(Km(1+[I]/Ki)+[S]) ≈ 0.445. The inhibitor binds ~42× tighter than substrate (Ki 34.3 µM vs Km 1446.6 µM), so even a low molar ratio produces ~55% inhibition.",
